5	   "where": "AC-111 (L1658) and Dependencies Kernel row (L535) vs LY-32 (L456)",
6	   "issue": "LY-32 and ADR-0013 section 8 add a fourth dirty-key kind, LEAF 4. The `layout.doors` hook marks one `LEAF/<section_id>` per section whose leaf set changed, so the PROJECTOR redraws the leaf. AC-111 still lists KIND as SEC 1, BODY 2, SEAM 3 and the key names as SEC, BODY and S only. L535 lists only the dirty keys `SEC/`, `BODY/`, `S/`. No AC anywhere asserts that `layout.doors` marks LEAF once per changed section, or that a rejected close marks none. An implementer following the AC list would ship a hook that marks no key, and the leaf sprite would not redraw (ADR-0013 section 8, TR-section-013).",
7	   "fix": "Amend AC-111 to KIND SEC 1, BODY 2, SEAM 3, LEAF 4, with `LEAF/<id>` encoded as `(4 << 32) | id`. Add one AC: GIVEN a `layout.doors` pass in which two doors of section 3 and one door of section 5 changed leaf WHEN it runs THEN exactly `LEAF/3` and `LEAF/5` are marked (once each), a pass with no leaf change marks none, and `static_version` is untouched. Add LEAF to the L535 dirty-key list. Mark each edit *(Amended 2026-10-29 — ADR-0013 sync)*."
8	  }
